{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "challenge_id": "lc_2286",
  "measurement_note": "Size is N = n + q, where n is the row count and q is the number of booking requests. Every tier uses n = q = N / 2, one seat per row, and q impossible gather(2, n - 1) calls. The segment tree rejects each request from its stored maximum without scanning rows, so construction plus all requests takes O((n + q) log n) time. A correct row-array implementation that searches every eligible row for each failed request completes all tiers and fails through O(nq) scaling.",
